Phase 22A: Install Gunicorn

Flask's built-in server is only for development.

Install:

Shell
source venv/bin/activate
 
pip install gunicorn

Verify:

Shell
gunicorn --version
Phase 22B: Test Gunicorn

Inside project folder:

Shell
cd ~/student_portal

Run:

Shell
gunicorn app:app

Output:

Plain Text
Listening at: http://127.0.0.1:8000

Open:

Plain Text
http://127.0.0.1:8000

Your application should work.

Phase 22C: Run on Network IP

Find Ubuntu IP:

Shell
ip addr

Or:

Shell
hostname -I

Example:

Plain Text
192.168.1.100

Run:

Shell
gunicorn --bind 0.0.0.0:8000 app:app

Now access:

Plain Text
http://192.168.1.100:8000

from another machine on the network.

Phase 22D: Install Nginx

Install:

Shell
sudo apt update
 
sudo apt install nginx -y

Verify:

Shell
sudo systemctl status nginx

Open browser:

Plain Text
http://localhost
 

You should see:

Plain Text
Welcome to nginx
Phase 22E: Configure Nginx

Create config:

Shell
sudo nano /etc/nginx/sites-available/student_portal

Paste:

Nginx Config
server {
 
listen 80;
 
server_name localhost;
 
location / {
 
proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000;
 
proxy_set_header Host $host;
 
proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
}
}

Save.

Enable Site
Shell
sudo ln -s \
/etc/nginx/sites-available/student_portal \
/etc/nginx/sites-enabled/

Check config:

Shell
sudo nginx -t

Expected:

Plain Text
syntax is ok
 

Restart:

Shell
sudo systemctl restart nginx
Phase 22F: Start Application

Terminal 1:

Shell
cd ~/student_portal
 
source venv/bin/activate
 
gunicorn --bind 127.0.0.1:8000 app:app

Terminal 2:

Shell
systemctl status nginx

Open:

Plain Text
http://localhost

Your Student Portal should appear.

Phase 22G: Run Gunicorn in Background
Shell
nohup gunicorn \
--bind 127.0.0.1:8000 \
app:app &

Check:

Shell
ps aux | grep gunicorn
Phase 22H: Open Firewall

If firewall is enabled:

Shell
sudo ufw allow 80

Check:

Shell
sudo ufw status
Phase 22I: HTTPS (Optional)

Install:

Shell
sudo apt install certbot \
python3-certbot-nginx -y

If you have a real domain:

Shell
sudo certbot --nginx

This enables:

Plain Text
https://your-domain.com
